    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37268" root="كنبث" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُنْبُثٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُنْبُوثٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُنَابثٌِ</span></b>  <i>Hard</i> (L, K)
<i>and strong.</i> (L.) [Epithets applied to a man.]
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, all the three words, <i>Contracted</i> [<i>in
disposition</i>], <i>and niggardly,</i> or <i>stingy.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
Mentioned before in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كبث</span>; and like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُلْبُثٌ</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [Accord. to the L, these epithets seem
also to apply to a man <i>Contracted in make:</i> the
first and third being expl. by the words <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَدَاخَلَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَعْضُهُ فِى بَعْضٍ</span>.]

